{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "papers": [
    {
      "id": "8c8e315d-55c9-4262-8a6d-b884ad2e06cb",
      "title": "From Components to Instances: Iterative Composition",
      "templateRef": {
        "id": "exploration",
        "version": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "id": "ada40061-3d12-4cf3-ba56-bda67cd92f32",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "level": 2,
            "isToggleable": false
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Abstract",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "501e8d35-83f7-4c1b-bc16-1dc0d6824d8d",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Working proposal only. This paper investigates whether repeated, constraint-guided composition can grow existing components into an intent-specific instance. No experimental findings are claimed.",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "343681cb-ff65-4db1-a5f6-1b862d368f93",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "level": 2,
            "isToggleable": false
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Introduction and Research Question",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "71412d7d-d70b-453a-b9a4-a79d475910c2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Which algorithm or combination of methods can most effectively use component capabilities, interfaces, dependencies, and constraints to iteratively produce viable composites and higher-layer assemblies until an instance satisfies its intent? Candidate approaches are not restricted to System 1 or System 2: deterministic algorithms, neural models, language-model reasoning, and hybrid methods are all in scope. The genetic makeup metaphor refers provisionally to the structured description of each component; its precise definition remains open.",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "636b7d9d-45c6-4df2-9e50-87e8b895e396",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "level": 2,
            "isToggleable": false
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Background and Related Work",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "34eab192-8366-404e-8da7-8e4de8a3b192",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Not researched yet.",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "9b8bb5c9-1762-43bb-ae77-579c4fbc3749",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "level": 2,
            "isToggleable": false
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Provisional Hypotheses and Predictions",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "8909c974-5608-4874-afb2-07fef6e06438",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "No method is selected yet. Candidate hypotheses: deterministic composition may perform well where rules and interfaces are complete; learned candidate selection may reduce search effort; model-based reasoning may help with ambiguous requirements or novel combinations; hybrid methods may combine these advantages. Each claim requires comparative evidence and may be rejected.",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "19027d7b-c434-413b-8082-cee8569e48a3",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "level": 2,
            "isToggleable": false
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Assumptions and Alternative Explanations",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "3dd44027-78da-4efd-be7f-149ea96968ba",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Open assumptions: component descriptions contain enough information to judge useful combinations; local compatibility can be supplemented by assembly-level behavior checks; repeated composition improves requirement coverage rather than merely adding layers. Compare against predefined recipes and unguided composition.",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "8ba3ee76-b71c-4351-ae30-baa9399ff44e",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "level": 2,
            "isToggleable": false
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Methods of Inquiry",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "b2a29ed8-1ce0-4bae-9493-0c8dcc3a2b00",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Define representative composition tasks, shared component libraries, validation checks, stopping rules, and equal resource budgets. Compare deterministic search and recipes, learned or neural candidate selection, language-model planning, and hybrid variants. Measure requirement satisfaction, valid assembly rate, unsupported assumptions, runtime success where execution is in scope, latency, cost, and reuse on held-out tasks. Keep evaluators independent of candidate generation. Reward measured outcomes rather than additional nodes or layers.",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "c696747a-797d-4723-b9a9-e9047c603999",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "level": 2,
            "isToggleable": false
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Results and Evidence",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "2a907a30-ef19-42df-9d4b-1f22b9f6a35f",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "No experiment has been run for this research question. Existing canvas demonstrations do not establish that this general algorithm works.",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "bde609b3-e067-4ea9-bbbd-fee3bee677dc",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "level": 2,
            "isToggleable": false
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Discussion and Critical Evaluation",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "b795e4ac-3801-492a-9c7d-f680ee57d5f2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "To be developed after defining the mechanism and collecting evidence.",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "3d6eb567-f039-4967-8c83-5d22ea4feed1",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "level": 2,
            "isToggleable": false
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Limitations and Validity",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "a6dfd1de-eef7-4c8c-a2f9-94ea43f8a74f",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Compatibility alone does not establish usefulness or correctness. More abstraction layers do not necessarily indicate progress. Hidden dependencies, inaccurate capability descriptions, and failed assumptions may prevent a viable assembly.",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "80bb6d7d-855a-452b-8776-d223080be12f",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "level": 2,
            "isToggleable": false
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Conclusion",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "e07417ef-a6a6-4fdd-83dc-bef53e44607c",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Unresolved. This is a research direction, not an established capability.",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "df33d747-a3a9-442f-bce3-b065f5ce3a64",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "level": 2,
            "isToggleable": false
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Open Questions and Next Tests",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "cfa1aecd-ce94-47b0-9d80-01bc69ce74c8",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "What exactly belongs in a component’s structured description? What is the minimum representative task set? Which outcomes and constraints define effectiveness, and how should quality, cost, latency, reliability, and reuse be balanced? What evidence establishes that an instance is substantial enough to stop? Specific model identities and capability claims mentioned in conversation require verification before becoming research premises.",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "9518cc5e-0cdd-4397-8b82-a77a8d9a4c22",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left",
            "level": 2,
            "isToggleable": false
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Reproducibility and Disclosures",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "9b1edb59-269b-4dd6-9db9-388cba70b0c8",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "backgroundColor": "default",
            "textColor": "default",
            "textAlignment": "left"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Initial idea supplied by the user; organization and provisional wording assisted by AI. No external literature review or experimental evaluation has yet been performed.",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ],
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "id": "668f7995-a67d-43d4-bb75-ccccf0b8efff",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
